From: Banks Troutman <banks.troutman@oxos.com>
Subject: make-sdcard: remove sudo fallback for unprivileged flash

Run as the invoking user — fail with EPERM instead of silently
escalating. User must have disk group access to the block device.

Make partprobe non-fatal: both partprobe and blockdev --rereadpt
require CAP_SYS_ADMIN on some kernels even with block device write
access. The initrd re-reads partitions independently.

--- a/make-sdcard.sh
+++ b/make-sdcard.sh
@@ -12,8 +12,6 @@
 HAVEBMAPTOOL=

 SUDO=
-[ $(id -u) -eq 0 ] || SUDO="sudo"
-
 usage() {
     cat <<EOF

@@ -451,10 +449,7 @@
 if [ -b "$output" ]; then
     sleep 1
-    if ! $SUDO partprobe "$output" >/dev/null 2>&1; then
-	echo "ERR: partprobe failed after partitioning $output" >&2
-	exit 1
-    fi
+    partprobe "$output" 2>/dev/null || blockdev --rereadpt "$output" 2>/dev/null || true
     sleep 1
 fi
